-- The product version is the `version` field of the table below.
-- 1.29.0: walks no longer stop and re-ask for a path. The 12 yd path segments (each ended in an
-- arrival, then awaiting_path) are off; walks of 15+ yd are planned first (plan_route), audited for
-- steep ground, then walked as follow_path; re-generation and the horizon (>= 20 yd of path ahead)
-- swap fresh paths in while walking; the quest engine hints the next waypoint (floors, audit and the
-- walk start a few yards early). Terrain avoidance: steep spans, ledges, drops, stuck points and
-- slots narrower than the body become Sentinel avoidance zones; one shared terrain model; stall log.
-- 1.28.147: a ghost takes no fall damage - steep descents and drops no longer
-- veto its route (ascent limits unchanged).
-- 1.28.146: corpse run no longer freezes on a guessed corpse height; the onward
-- route check compares x/y only when the corpse z is a fallback guess.
-- 1.28.5: verify trainer class before travel, gossip selection or purchases;
-- unknown trainers no longer match every class.
-- 1.28.4: lateral-only Rogue strafing; short indoor and elevation-change
-- floor checks; tighter indoor target matching and three-dimensional arrival.
-- 1.28.3: stale inventory-full events cannot start another vendor trip when
-- current bags have free slots; clear loot attempt history on Stop/reset.
-- 1.28.2: let Sentinel own running-path validation; remove private check_path
-- polling that repeatedly restarted live paths every three seconds.
-- 1.28.1: published as the active Forever Questing card 3 product again.
-- 1.28.0: a mage attacks the enemy with Frostbolt / Fireball from spell
-- range. Melee auto-attack is armed only in melee (starting Attack from 30
-- yards made the client run in and cancel the cast). A wand is started only
-- when one is equipped and mana is below the wand slider.
-- 1.27.0: loot at 2 yards; vendor trips use RestedXP vendor locations only
-- (never a random flagged NPC); class trainer every 3 levels is the closest
-- RestedXP Forever .trainer step.
-- 1.26.0: Auto Equip on by default; body armour is worn only when this class
-- can use that type at this level. A piece with no readable type is skipped.
-- 1.25.0: bags full and unable to loot force a walk to the nearest vendor.
-- 1.24.0: Stop and GUI close fully halt the bot (force Sentinel stop, attack off).
-- `folder` is the key for NS._sessions (a freshly loaded instance tells an
-- older one still ticking that it has been superseded); it carries no version
-- so a hot reload from one release to the next keeps the same key.
-- Authors: BLIZZ - Anthonyk
-- 1.22.0: the ray self-check no longer condemns the client on ONE missing ray (ported from Auto BG 2.62.0; session log 2026-10-28, Warsong Gulch: "Ray helpers switched off for this session: self-check: a ray through the ground under the player did not hit" in both plugin loads, which left the local A* fallback off for the whole match). A trace_line that THROWS is a broken client and still switches rays off at once; a trace_line that ANSWERS FALSE only says that one segment hit nothing, and a miss is expected in the air after a jump or a knock-back, swimming, riding a lift or on a thin WMO edge. The SAMPLE must be trustworthy before its answer counts - not falling, not swimming, not flying (game_object is_falling / is_swimming / is_flying and core.character.is_swimming, all in the live stub) - it takes 5 misses from such positions 2 s apart to switch rays off, a budget or error answer (nil) is not counted as a miss, and the ground segment reaches +2 / -5 yd instead of +1.5 / -2. Test: tests/test_ray_selfcheck.lua, which asserts all five copies.
--
-- 1.21.0: the self-centred AoE count (Arcane Explosion, Blast Wave, Whirlwind, Consecration, Holy Nova...). smart.lua's aoe_count took the spell_prediction answer whole; a self-centred spell's circle is drawn ON the player and get_circle_list answers everything that geometry covers - spell_data carries exception_player_included / exception_target_included and what the module does with them by default is in no stub, so the player and the pet could make up 2 of a 3-enemy threshold and fire an area spell at a single mob. The bot's own pack count (c.near, enemies only) now caps a self-centred prediction; a ground or target-centred circle is somewhere else, so its prediction still stands alone. Ported from Zygor Questing 1.46.0. Test: tests/test_aoe_counts.lua
--
-- 1.20.0: the step automation diagnostics (audit F7), ported from Zygor Questing: quest/diag.lua logs step transitions with the goal ledger of the step being left (done / held / open and which goals were open), goal transitions, an arrow tally by type, corpse runs, and a summary line every 2 minutes while something is changing. A goal this product is holding itself (guide.defer) is counted apart from an open goal, so a deferred goal is not read as a step that moved on its own. LOGGING ONLY - it owns no state the engine reads, no decision consults it, and every call site is in a pcall. Read a session with: grep diag <scripts_log>/MASTER_FARMER_ERRORS/session_*.log
-- 1.10.0 (Desktop items_db): Healthstones at the potion line, 3 foods / drinks added.
-- 1.10.1 (Desktop Helper): a swift mount item beats a slow class mount; Golden Pearl kept.
-- 1.11.0: the ray walk assistant (movement/trace.lua from Desktop Helper trace.lua; user lifted the ray rule): Sentinel walking with no progress and the way ahead blocked - a low obstacle is jumped, a wall gets a Sentinel avoidance zone and a soft re-plan.
-- 1.10.2: repeated countdown status lines (spellbook wait, corpse walk, approach) print at most every 5 s.
-- 1.14.0 (user: "use A* + rays alongside Sentinel navigation to improve player navigation"): the local A* + ray fallback (movement/astar.lua, ported from Zygor) runs alongside Sentinel - when a Sentinel walk ends "arrived" short of its goal or "unreachable" within 15 yd, a short local grid path is searched with game raycasts and walked leg by leg through Sentinel move_direct (N.astar_leg, never a key). General tab "Local A* Fallback" (fq_astar), on by default; AS.ON kill switch, per-frame ray budget, self-check, off for the session after repeated ray/height errors. Sentinel is never replaced - additive.
-- ============================================================================
-- 1.13.0: bag items that start or finish quests (quest/bagstart.lua, same file in Zygor and RestedXP): ".use" goals are handled (quest.item_goal: the goal's item, else the step's item / a quest starter while the step accepts a quest; used at the waypoint, 6 uses then set aside), the quest panel an item opens is accepted, and an accept with no guide data for its item is started from the bags (quest.bag_start).
-- 1.12.0: the ray helpers (movement/trace.lua) gain the Orca A* port's logic (user 2026-10-26): hit_z (8-step impact height), ground_z (height query, else a ray snap), a jump only with headroom over the obstacle and no drop past 6 yd behind it (else an avoidance zone), a corner snag at the side gets a small zone.
-- 1.15.0: the GUI window id no longer carries the product version (user 2026-10-27: "Product versions have changed, GUI resolution is no longer applied"). Every release minted a NEW core.menu.window id, so the saved window size / position / active tab were dropped and the window reopened at the hard-coded 1100 x 640 1080p default while mf_skin drew the artwork at the screen's real pixel scale. The id is fixed now (as mf_route_tool has always had), and a window opened for the first time takes mf_skin.window_px for this screen. This release migrates the id once - the window starts fresh a final time, then keeps its geometry.
-- 1.16.0: check_path (advanced Sentinel API, user 2026-10-27): while a walk of ours runs, the path Sentinel is following is validated every 3 s and an unambiguous "no longer valid" takes a fresh path at once instead of waiting for the walk to stall into the stuck ladder. nav_client:check_path is present on v0.24 but its callback shape is NOT recorded, so the adapter only acts on an explicit valid=false / blocked=true / reachable=false - a bare false (what a server error looks like here) answers "no opinion" and never re-plans; the first answer's shape is logged so the real shape can be read back. Never on a fresh leg or with a path request in flight (the crash rule), never through a hold or a pending stop. 3 throws, or a library without check_path, switch it off for the session.
-- 1.17.0: always dismount for a doorway, measured with the mounted player height
-- (user: "Always dismount when attempting to enter doorways, use get player height
-- when mounted, to check entrances to keep player from getting stuck"). get_height()
-- answers the body we have right now, so mounted it IS the taller body. movement/trace
-- remembers the on-foot height whenever is_mounted() is false and, while mounted,
-- probes 1 / 2 / 3 yd ahead at three heights: clear at the waist and at the on-foot
-- head (the player fits) but blocked at the mounted head (the mount does not) is a
-- doorway, and movement/mount M.dismount takes us off at once and suppresses mounting
-- for 8 s so M.step does not put us straight back into it. Blocked at the waist too is
-- a WALL, left to the wall logic, and a flying mount is never dismounted in the air.
-- The check runs while the walk is still MOVING, unlike the jump / wall checks which
-- only look after a stall: the point is to be short before the doorway rather than to
-- notice after being wedged in it. Sentinel is not stopped for it and keeps its path.
-- 1.18.0: the Sentinel kite retreat survives a target switch (found in Zygor
-- Questing 1.42.0; movement/combat.lua is shared, so the bug was here too).
-- combat_engage's per-target reset zeroed st.retreat_until and st.kite_pending, so
-- the hold above the "range <= reach" branch stopped applying and the kite walk was
-- stopped as "in range" on the new attacker about a second after it started - which
-- in a multi-mob fight is continuously. nav_client:kite was answering all along; the
-- retreat was simply being thrown away. A retreat is about where the PLAYER needs to
-- be, not which unit is being hit, so it now outlives the switch and ends on its own
-- RETREAT_TIME. The latch and band state still reset per target.
-- 1.19.0: audit phase 1 - the death loop, and a UI reload that was never there.
--   DEATH ZONES (audit F5, from session_2026-10-27_20-56-27.log: the character died
--   6 times in 11 minutes in Zangarmarsh and a zone never armed once - every death
--   logged "death 1 in this area ... 3 needed to avoid it"). A death joined a group
--   only if it was BOTH within JOIN_YARDS (60) AND killed by the SAME npc id, and 3
--   were needed. The log shows both halves failing: deaths 3 and 4 were 27 yd apart
--   in one Bloodscale camp but to different mobs (18089 / 18088), and deaths 4 and 5
--   were the same mob 94 yd apart. A bot dying to a mixed camp or a patrol - the
--   normal case - could never reach 3, so the protection was dead code while the
--   guide re-issued the identical waypoint five times and walked back in. Grouping is
--   AREA ONLY now (the killer npc is still recorded, for the zone's label and for
--   KILLER_PAD) and two deaths are enough. Against that log it arms at death 2 and
--   again at death 4. A repeat death in an area extends the zone that is there
--   instead of stacking a second one on it. tests/test_deathzones_group.lua replays
--   all five real deaths; it fails 18 assertions on the old logic.
--   PERIODIC UI RELOAD REMOVED (audit F1): core.reload_game_ui is declared in NO
--   local stub - absent from all nine .api copies under Documents (2026-10-16 ..
--   2026-10-27), from sylvanas_api/.api and from BLIZZ_PROJECTS/.api, and so are
--   core.reload_plugins and core.reload_scripts. The 30-minute reload and the fifteen
--   safety checks that guarded it therefore never did anything except cost a check
--   per frame. Removed rather than left as a guarded call to a function that is
--   nowhere; the comment in main.lua says how to put it back if a build ever
--   declares one.
